          "letter": "F",
          "english": "\"I don't think there's anything wrong with an audience showing their enthusiasm for a proper moment by applauding, showing their joy,\" Greenberg said, noting that the stuffiness in concert halls is \"one aspect of contemporary concert etiquette\" he doesn't understand. \"Instead of waiting half an hour to show enthusiasm, why not show it every eight or nine minutes?\"",
