          "number": 8,
          "letter": "H",
          "english": "Greenberg stressed that he doesn't want people to start respecting the music less, and he's not suggesting that we \"dumb down\" the experience. Rather, it's about opening up \"access.\" When operas first instituted subtitles(字幕) during shows, he said, many purists didn't like the idea, believing that the audience should instead study the works before attending. But now it's commonplace to find titles on the seatback in front of you—choose a language, sit back, and understand what's going on.",
          "chinese": "格林伯格强调，他并不希望人们减少对音乐的尊重，也不是在建议我们把这种体验“降低难度”。相反，关键在于扩大“接触的机会”。他说，歌剧演出最初采用字幕时，许多守旧派并不喜欢这个想法，认为观众应该在入场前先研究作品。但如今，在你前方座椅的靠背上看到字幕已经很普遍了——选择一种语言，坐下来，然后理解正在发生什么。",
