          "number": 9,
          "letter": "I",
          "english": "Allison Vulgamore, president of the Philadelphia Orchestra, is certainly looking to the future. She says certain \"classics concerts\" dedicated to the old masters will always exist, but not every program has to feature Beethoven and Brahms—or even a stage and seats. \"We're trying to introduce different kinds of concerts in different ways,\" she said. \"We are an interactive society now, where people like to learn.\"",
          "chinese": "费城交响乐团团长艾莉森·武尔加莫无疑正在着眼于未来。她说，专门献给古代大师作品的某些“经典音乐会”将始终存在，但并不是每个节目都必须安排贝多芬和勃拉姆斯的作品，甚至也不一定要有舞台和座位。“我们正努力以不同的方式推出不同类型的音乐会，”她说。“我们现在生活在一个互动型社会中，人们喜欢学习。”",
