          "english": "Greenberg thinks that youthful energy needs to be harvested. Conductors don't have to be arrogant and untouchable—they can be accessible. Perhaps there could even be a \"bit of humor\" about them, he suggested, and an abandoning of pretension within the high-art institutions themselves. \"On one hand, these organizations are all saying the same thing: we want more general audiences, to break down cultural barriers,\" he said. \"But then they come up with some very snooty(目中无人的) thing that makes you crazy.\"",
