          "number": 2,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "Deep within the genetic heart of all our cells are telomeres, or repeating segments of noncoding DNA that live at the ends of the chromosomes(染色体). They form caps at the ends of the chromosomes and keep the genetic material together. Shortening with each cell division, they help determine how fast a cell ages. When they become too short, the cell stops dividing altogether. This isn't the only reason a cell can age—there are other stresses on cells we don't yet understand very well—but short telomeres are one of the major reasons human cells grow old. We've devoted most of our careers to studying telomeres, and one extraordinary discovery from our labs is that telomeres can actually lengthen.",
          "chinese": "在我们所有细胞的遗传核心深处，存在着端粒，也就是位于染色体末端的、重复排列的非编码DNA片段。它们在染色体末端形成帽状结构，使遗传物质保持完整。端粒会随着每次细胞分裂而缩短，并帮助决定细胞衰老的速度。当端粒变得过短时，细胞就会完全停止分裂。这并不是细胞衰老的唯一原因——细胞还会受到其他我们尚未充分了解的压力——但端粒过短是人类细胞衰老的主要原因之一。我们职业生涯的大部分时间都致力于研究端粒，而我们实验室的一项非凡发现是，端粒实际上能够变长。",
